From 671a38bb64dd30ec283d37a02cbb2a70a3b9a44b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Move the tooling into src/: the repo root is the site,
 src/ is what makes it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The root mixed three kinds of things: the site GitHub Pages serves (index,
404, slides/, engine/, resources/, transcripts/), the deck sources (src/)
and the machinery around them (build.js, package.json, bun.lock, tests/,
the two Python tools). Now everything that is not the site lives in src/,
next to the sources it builds from — src/presentations/ and src/slides/
stay where they are, so every @include path is unchanged — and the root
keeps the Makefile as the one entry point.

- build.js resolves the repo root as its parent directory; build(root)
  and the include root (src/) are unchanged
- the e2e server serves the repo root from three levels up; the narration
  fixture is now at /src/tests/e2e/fixtures/
- the Makefile runs every bun one-liner from src/ (`cd src && bun run …`);
  the workflow reads the Playwright version there
- .gitignore, README, tests/e2e/README.md and the Python tools' docstrings
  follow the paths

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
